<title>USA: Nationwide Financial sells $300 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Nationwide Financial sells $300 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Nationwide Financial Services Inc was priced Wednesday, according to co-lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co was also co-lead manager.</p>
<p>BORROWER NATIONWIDE FINANCIAL SERVICES</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 8.00 PCT   MATURITY 3/01/2027</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.455  FIRST PAY DATE 9/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 8.048 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 112.5 BP   CALLABLE NON CALL 10</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
